Subject: I-N: Group Dynamics and a Question for Harry

First a question for Harry...

While the extropian mailing list (the names) might be considered
proprietary, I was wondering how many people (the cardinality) were on
it.  While I have a feel for the number of "active" participants, I
wonder how many "lurkers" are out there.  It's much like conducting a
discussion in a darkened auditorium-- hard to know how many seats are
occupied (and by whom).  From Paul Cisek's survey results it appears
that with few exceptions that most of the respondants were already
known to us through their postings.  Their "credentials" also come as
no suprise to anyone who has followed the discussions.

And now a follow up ...

Many years ago I read of some experiments having to do with "Group IQ"
as a function of group organization and size.  More recently I
participated in a "workshop" which demonstrated this phenomenon.  I
