Friends, Angelenos, Car-Nuts, Lend me your ears...

I was scared this weekend.  Amazing but true, I am one of a few
people that I know that is *not* carrying a side-arm in the car.
Those in my family and a few of my friends may find this shocking,
but I hope to continue this until actual violence starts.

I want to put this in writing, and I hope that it makes some sense.

I am considered among some of peers an "expert" (though my relatives
would giggle at that notion, since they are *real* experts) in
firearms, and their lethal use.  Part of my reasoning to own a lethal
weapon is that I consider it moraly correct to *kill* anything that
threatens myself, my family or my rights (1st-10th).  I have made this
decision and sleep very well with it.  Note the word kill.  If
something threatens me, I will kill it.  That prevents it from *ever*
threatening me again.

I have a problem with people who own guns to protect themselves.  The
problem is a linguistic one, yet it points to my problem with most
people's gun ownership habits.

If you own the gun to kill people while protecting yourself, that
means that the purpose of the gun is to kill.  The role of the gun is
clearly defined and you have clearly thought the whole process
through.  Injuring the person does not solve the imeadiate problem,
it moves it to a future time (minute, if he can recover, years if he
is convicted).  Killing them solves the problem.

By saying that you have a gun with you, or in your car, "for
protection" says the you:

    1. Intend to use it as a threat to hold the other person at bay,
       or scare them.
    2. You think the mere presence of a gun in your hand will prevent
       trouble.
    3. You might not kill when the chips are down.

A gun in the hands of a person that does not intend to protect
themselves by killing is an empty threat.  The other person will kill
you with some weapon before you pull the trigger, or you will fire
and miss (since it is not your intention to harm your attacker).  You
only chance of "success" lies in the belief that your attacker is
somehow rational enough to recognize their mortality and follow your
instructions and stay for the police.  This is unlikely.  You must
assume that rational people do not brandish weapons and attempt to
violate other people and their property.  Ask yourself "do rational
people generally engage in unlawful behavior like car-jacking,
breaking-and-entering, assult, etc, etc?" Or are this people
irrational, and therefore unlikely to follow your instructions or
respond to your threat.  Unrational people will harm you, inspite of
your gun.

If you do intend to kill in protecting your life and liberty, then
the question of carrying guns in your car is a tactical one.
Assuming that you adhear to the current laws on transportation of
firearms, then getting to your gun in time to prevent anything or
kill any threat is impractical.  You will be dead before you ever get
to your gun and your attacker will have another weapon to use on
someone else.  Want proof? Sit in your car with your gun in the place
where you intend to keep your gun.  Now try to unholster, load and
point the gun within a count of three.  If you can, you might have a
chance, otherwise, your irrational attacker will kill you.

If you can do this, you are probably in violation of the vehical code
on transporting a firearm.  And I doubt that you will be able to
effectively aim and fire the gun.  You will be injured by glass,
shrapnel, and whatever else, and you might end up on trial for "man-
slaughter" since you carried the gun illegally.

Finally, if you are pulled over and searched, you will be charged
with carrying a loaded or concealed weapon in your car.  Most likely,
during the riots, their will be traffic breaks and cars will be
searched.  If you are carrying, and you could concievably get to your
weapon, load it, in a count of three, the police will arrest you.

Therefore, the rational choice is not to carry a gun in your car.

How do you protect yourself?  Listen to the radio in your car and
avoid areas of trouble.  Make sure your car is mechanically sound.

If you are in a dangerous area, make a plan to get out quickly, and
allow plenty of space between you and other cars.  If you get in a
threatening situation, duck, hit the gas, and run.  If they kill you,
then you are dead.  A gun could not have saved you.

However, odds are that they cannot shoot thier weapon accurately, and
will not be able to hit your moving steel target and you will make it
out injured, but safe.

I hope that someone listens, and I would love for everyone on this
list to make this document available to anyone that they know that
has started to carry a gun in their car/truck.  If nothing else, I
would appreciate the distribution (anoymously, please) in the hope of
spreading some sanity.


